            <ArticleTitle>[Causes for consultation in the emergency room among patients with systemic autoimmune diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1546-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4067/S0034-98872015001200007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0034-98872015001200007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The causes of acute decompensations of patients with systemic autoimmune diseases are not well known.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe the causes for consultation in an emergency room of patients with systemic autoimmune diseases.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Review of medical records of patients with systemic autoimmune diseases, aged over 14 years, consulting in an emergency room of a general hospital during three months.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In the study period, 166 patients with systemic autoimmune diseases consulted in the emergency room, of a total of 18,153 consultations (0.9%). Patients with rheumatoid arthritis were those that consulted with higher frequency (37%) followed by patients with systemic lupus erythematosus (21%). The most common causes for consultation were cardiovascular diseases in 25%, followed by digestive disorders in 15%. The most common diagnosis was chest pain with suspected ischemic heart disease in 36%. No differences in cardiovascular risk factors were observed between those patients consulting for cardiovascular diseases and those consulting for other causes.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The most common cause of consultation in the emergency room of patients with systemic autoimmune diseases is cardiovascular.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
